          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is built for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then gives a human admin an approve, reject, or request-info recommendation with its reasons.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but can never approve one.\n\nThe project is in offline evals, with deployment next. Across 31 test cases, the team picked Claude Haiku 5.5 for deployment over a local 9B model. Haiku reached 86% accuracy versus 71%, and let through 1% of fraud versus 8%. It costs about $0.002 per review. The stack is TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP.",
